course: dictionary
lesson: 3631
title: Finger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A finger is one of the five long parts at the end of your hand. The thumb is often counted separately, so each hand has four fingers and a thumb. «Keep your fingers away from the fan blades» means you could get hurt if you put them near the moving blades.
explain: Finger can also name something shaped like a finger, such as «fish fingers». As a verb, to finger something means to touch or feel it with your fingers. Context tells you which meaning is used: is it a body part, a food, or an action?
explain: Read «A boy in Texas woke his hamster in the daytime by poking it; the startled hamster bit his finger hard.» Finger is a body part here, because it is the thing that got bitten. In «Fish fingers are usually white fish cut into blocks», finger means a food shaped like a finger. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
fact: A finger is one of the long parts at the end of your hand.
fact: «Fish fingers» are fish cut into finger-shaped blocks and breadcrumbed; they were first sold in Britain in 1955.
fact: Every person's fingerprints are different, and fingers have nails.
fact: Ten fingers are one reason we count in tens.
fact: A fish hook stuck in a finger must not be pulled out, because its barb tears the skin; an adult or doctor removes it.
exercise: «Fish fingers» are a food. What does finger mean in this phrase? | A part of the hand | A small fish with long fins | To touch with the fingers | *Something shaped like a finger
exercise: «The startled hamster bit his finger hard.» What is his finger? | A type of food | *One of the long parts at the end of his hand | A hook on a fish | A kind of hamster
exercise: Amira wants to know how the soft cloth feels, so she decides to finger it. What does finger mean here? | To count to ten | To cut into blocks | To point at with a stick | *To touch or feel with the fingers
test: How many fingers and toes does one child have, if 3 children have 60 altogether? | 5 | 30 | *20 | 10
test: What is a fingerprint? | A barb on the point of a hook | A hamster's bite | *A mark made by a fingertip that is different for every person | A block of breadcrumbed fish
exam: «A fish hook stuck in a finger is not pulled out; an adult or doctor removes it.» Why must an adult or doctor remove it? | Because fingers are too small to hold them | Because the hook is shaped like a finger | Because hooks are only for fish | *Because the barb tears the skin
